Subject: [PATCH] venus: destroy the context's ring mutex after the ring monitor

vkr_context_destroy destroyed ctx->ring_mutex before it stopped the ring monitor, whose thread
locks that mutex (vkr_context_ring_monitor_thread). On bionic a lock of a destroyed mutex aborts
the render server ("FORTIFY: pthread_mutex_lock called on a destroyed mutex"), as in patch 0006;
only at teardown, but with a tombstone.

Destroy the mutex after the ring monitor's end.

---
--- a/src/venus/vkr_context.c
+++ b/src/venus/vkr_context.c
@@ -623,13 +623,15 @@
       vkr_ring_stop(ring);
       vkr_ring_destroy(ring);
    }
-   mtx_destroy(&ctx->ring_mutex);
 
    vkr_context_wait_ring_fini(ctx);
 
    if (ctx->ring_monitor.started)
       vkr_context_ring_monitor_fini(ctx);
 
+   /* after the ring monitor, whose thread locks it */
+   mtx_destroy(&ctx->ring_mutex);
+
    if (ctx->instance) {
       vkr_log("destroying context %d (%s) with a valid instance", ctx->ctx_id,
               vkr_context_get_name(ctx));
